<article class="env-proposition" id="00ZM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00ZM">Proposition <span data-tag="00ZM">7.49.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category endowed with a topology. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a presheaf of sets on $\mathcal{C}$. The canonical map $\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{F}^\# $ has the following universal property: For any map $\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{G}$, where $\mathcal{G}$ is a sheaf of sets, there is a unique map $\mathcal{F}^\#  \to \mathcal{G}$ such that $\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{F}^\#  \to \mathcal{G}$ equals the given map. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
